e lower-middle of the scale below Chadlite, and are used for faces seen as ordinary rather than especially attractive or unattractive.[1][2]","Within looksmaxxing the labels work as a starting point: a user who describes himself as an MTN or HTN base asks which changes could lift him, such as weight gain, grooming or fitness.[2] Other members reply with their own ratings, and replies sometimes dispute the placement, for example by calling a self-rating delusional.[2]","PSL is informal and not validated by research; tier boundaries differ between raters and threads, and no study has tested them."],"infobox":[["Framework","PSL scale (Perceived Sexual Levels)"],["Abbreviations","MTN, LTN"],["Position","Lower-middle, below Chadlite"],["Validation","Informal, unvalidated"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["Mid and low tier normie are bands of the PSL scale, which has its own wiki entry. Members use them when rating photos and when describing where they started.[1][2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"In looksmaxxing culture","paras":["Thread titles on looksmax.org include requests to be rated as MTN or LTN, and questions about whether MTN is enough when combined with height.[2][3] Members describe a self-improvement plan from an MTN base, and others reply with blunt assessments.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Mtn or ltn","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/mtn-or-ltn.1801549/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2025,"type":"forum"},{"title":"Mtn/Htn base help me","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/mtn-htn-base-help-me.1790526/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2025,"type":"forum"},{"title":"mtn is enough if u have height and ur nt","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/mtn-is-enough-if-u-have-height-and-ur-nt.1764286/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2025,"type":"forum"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Mtn or ltn","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/mtn-or-ltn.1801549/","site":"